.TH SAMBAM 1 "February 2026" "sambam" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sambam \- instant SMB/CIFS file sharing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sambam
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ directory ]
.br
.B sambam
.B stop
.br
.B sambam
.B status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sambam
starts a lightweight SMB server to share local directories with Windows, macOS, and Linux clients.
By default, it shares the current directory using the directory name as share name.
.SH CONFIGURATION
When
.B -c, --config
is not used, configuration is loaded in this order, with later layers overriding keys set earlier:
.IP "1." 4
.I /etc/sambamrc
.IP "2." 4
.I ~/.sambamrc
.IP "3." 4
.I ./.sambamrc
.PP
When
.B -c, --config
is used, default discovery is disabled and only explicit config files are loaded in the order passed.
.PP
Command-line flags override all config file values.
.PP
On startup, sambam reports loaded config files in concise form, for example:
.IP
.I config: loaded /etc/sambamrc, /root/.sambamrc, .sambamrc
.PP
or:
.IP
.I config: loaded none
.PP
Global config keys under
.B [global]
include:
.IP "\(bu" 4
.B allow
(default:
.I ["0.0.0.0/0"]
, allow all clients)
.IP "\(bu" 4
.B smb3_encryption
(default:
.I true
, used when client supports SMB3 encryption)
.IP "\(bu" 4
.B guest_browse_ipc
(default:
.I true
, allows guest IPC$/browse for discovery while share ACLs are still enforced)
.IP "\(bu" 4
.B show_connect_hints
(default:
.I true
, shows Windows/macOS/Linux connect commands in startup banner)
.IP "\(bu" 4
.B discovery_name_mdns
(default:
.I "<hostname>-sambam"
)
.IP "\(bu" 4
.B discovery_name_wsd
(default:
.I "<hostname>"
)
.IP "\(bu" 4
.B advertise
(default:
.I true
)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR "-n, --name" " <name|name:path>"
Share name or name:path pair. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR "-l, --listen" " <address>"
Listen address (default: 0.0.0.0:445). Supports IP:port or @interface[:port]. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR "-a, --allow" " <ip-or-cidr>"
Allow client IP/CIDR. Repeatable. Default allows all clients.
.TP
.BR "-x, --no-advertise"
Disable share advertisement (mDNS/WSD).
.TP
.BR "-r, --readonly"
Make share read-only.
.TP
.BR "-u, --username" " <user|user:password>"
Require authentication. Repeatable for multiple users.
.TP
.BR "-p, --password" " <password>"
Authentication password for single-user mode.
.TP
.BR "-e, --expire" " <duration>"
Auto-shutdown after duration (for example: 30m, 1h, 2h30m).
.TP
.BR "-v, --verbose"
Show activity logs. Use -vv for extended logs and -vvv for full trace.
.TP
.BR "-H, --hide-dotfiles"
Hide files starting with '.' from listings.
.TP
.BR "-d, --daemon"
Run in background. Stop with
.B sambam stop
.
.TP
.BR "-P, --pidfile" " <path>"
PID file path (default: /tmp/sambam.pid).
.TP
.BR "-L, --logfile" " [path]"
Log file path. Defaults to
.I /tmp/sambam.log
when value is omitted.
.TP
.BR "-c, --config" " <path>"
Load explicit config file(s). Repeatable. Disables default config discovery.
.TP
.BR "-G, --gen-config" " [path]"
Generate TOML config from current CLI flags and exit without starting the server.
Default output path is
.I ./.sambamrc
when omitted.
.TP
.BR "-V, --version"
Show version and exit.
.TP
.BR "-h, --help"
Show help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Share current directory:
.B sambam
.TP
Share a specific directory:
.B sambam /path/to/folder
.TP
Share read-only:
.B sambam -r /data
.TP
Run as daemon:
.B sambam -d /data
.br
.B sambam stop
.br
.B sambam status
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sambamrc
System-wide configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.sambamrc
User configuration.
.TP
.I ./.sambamrc
Project-local overrides.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non-zero on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount.cifs (8),
.BR smbclient (1)
